Yes, your understanding is completely correct!

Neither reserve_dev_alias() nor release_dev_alias() relies on the
checkpointed state of previous operations.
They only depend on the in-memory metadata (extent tree, SIT bitmaps,
i_size, etc.), which is already atomically updated and fully
synchronized by inode_lock and f2fs_lock_op.
Therefore, the interleaved checkpoint scenario you described won't
cause any issue at all.

